me.  Still, the first half or so of the book is very good, and full of wonderful gems."},{"owner":{"account_id":67941,"reputation":373,"user_id":144,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/3321e3f5894bfc21bb2c07f645181187?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"walkytalky","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/144/walkytalky"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1279766343,"post_id":358,"comment_id":665,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"@user80 Obviously I disagree - except about those critiques being weak..."},{"owner":{"account_id":176975,"reputation":6055,"user_id":16,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":58,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/ff748121af52550c6356b569ca740023?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"BBischof","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/16/bbischof"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1279752357,"post_id":364,"comment_id":594,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"One danger worth mentioning is that Nahin&#39;s books are full of mistakes and inaccuracies. He is known for &quot;lying&quot; about certain things that he perceives as too difficult to explain, rather than alerting the reader. In addition to this, he is absolutely uninterested in fixing these errors in later editions of his books, even when compact solutions are noted."},{"owner":{"account_id":71748,"reputation":4646,"user_id":80,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/ZuPqNhmS.jpg?s=256","display_name":"Dan Piponi","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/80/dan-piponi"},"edited":false,"score":4,"creation_date":1279735743,"post_id":358,"comment_id":512,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"There are good reasons not to recommend this book, especially to a non-mathematician who is as yet unaware of alternative points of view. Some reasons why are listed <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Mathematician%27s_Apology#Critiques\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">here</a>. I personally think those critiques are weak compared to what could be said."},{"owner":{"account_id":85546,"reputation":8794,"user_id":136,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":73,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/SINHF.png?s=256","display_name":"BlueRaja - Danny Pflughoeft","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/136/blueraja-danny-pflughoeft"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1279734061,"post_id":339,"comment_id":509,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Reading this right now, it&#39;s great"},{"owner":{"account_id":67941,"reputation":373,"user_id":144,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/3321e3f5894bfc21bb2c07f645181187?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"walkytalky","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/144/walkytalky"},"edited":false,"score":4,"creation_date":1279731296,"post_id":355,"comment_id":494,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"+1 for <b>GEB</b>, still one of my real <i>acid test</i> books after all these years."},{"owner":{"account_id":155827,"reputation":1485,"user_id":115,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/9a6a3cee904fe58146bea114d1948fca?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"user115","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/115/user115"},"edited":false,"score":3,"creation_date":1279721713,"post_id":323,"comment_id":462,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Martin Gardner is the gold standard. His columns are available on CD from the MAA and are also being reprinted in the New Martin Gardner Mathematical Library."}],"has_more":false,"quota_max":300,"quota_remaining":254}